--TEST--
A written `foreach` binding type is no target for an array literal subject, so the literal is `array<mixed>`, and the mismatch's help names `as var` and a typed array declared first — `rule:types/arrays`, `rule:types/var-inference`
--FILE--
<?nvs
foreach (['a', 'b'] as string $x) {
    echo $x, "\n";
}
foreach ([1, 2] as int $n) {
    echo $n, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `mixed`
  --> case.nvs:2:%d
%A
  = help: an array written directly in `foreach` has `mixed` items. Write `as var $x` to use the type of its items, or declare the array first: `array<string> $items = [...];`
%A
error[E0401]: expected `int`, found `mixed`
  --> case.nvs:5:%d
%A
  = help: an array written directly in `foreach` has `mixed` items. Write `as var $n` to use the type of its items, or declare the array first: `array<int> $items = [...];`
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
